{"meta":{"format_version":"4.10","model_format":"free","box_uv":false},"name":"runkin_drying_rack","model_identifier":"runkin_drying_rack","visible_box":[1,1,0],"variable_placeholders":"","variable_placeholder_buttons":[],"timeline_setups":[],"unhandled_root_fields":{"description":"# runkin_drying_rack\n\nRunkin drying rack: a pole frame lashed with sinew, strips of meat and split fish hanging to dry.\n\n- Footprint: 4 x 2 columns (64 x 32 units, 1.80 x 0.90 m), centred on the origin, front (door side) faces -Z.\n- Finished bounds: x -32..32, y 0..44, z -2..2 units.\n- Texture: 64 x 128, 1 px per unit, square pixels, nearest filtering. Every visible face has its own texture region painted with its material at world position (seams line up across faces); identical faces share a region; construction and ruined pieces map into the region of the face they were cut from. No cube is cut to fit the texture.\n- Cubes: finished 17, construction_0 5, construction_33 5, construction_66 5, ruined 8 (0 rotated: roof slabs and a few leaning props).\n\n## Hit box\n\n- 64 x 46 x 6 centred at the origin\n\n## State group sets (children of `root`; show exactly one)\n\n- `finished`: the finished building (visible by default).\n- `construction_0`, `construction_33`, `construction_66`: build progress at 0 %, 33 % and 66 % (staked outline and scaffold, then walls rising inside scaffold, then full frame with roof rafters).\n- `ruined`: collapsed shell, broken walls, rubble, fallen roof (use with `_damaged.png`, or `_abandoned.png` for F7 abandoned buildings).\n- `runkin_drying_rack_damaged.png`: damaged texture (scorch, holes, cracks) for the same UVs; works on every group set.\n- `runkin_drying_rack_abandoned.png`: abandoned look (damage plus moss, faded cloth, cold fires) = `abandoned_runkin_drying_rack` together with the `ruined` set or the finished set.\n"},"resolution":{"width":64,"height":128},"elements":[{"name":"post0","box_uv":false,"rescale":false,"locked":false,"light_emission"